Backport of the lost-wakeup fix in ConfigLoader::updateConfigThread() from
upstream commit 2d7d08c3f715 (https://github.com/pytorch/kineto/pull/1531).

stopThread() sets stopFlag_ before it notifies, so a notify that lands while
the poll thread is still on its way into the bare wait_for() goes unheard, and
the join waits for a full poll interval (300 s). It makes
ConfigLoaderPollThreadExceptionTest time out under Bazel's default test timeout.

--- a/libkineto/src/ConfigLoader.cpp
+++ b/libkineto/src/ConfigLoader.cpp
@@ -252,7 +252,8 @@
         system_clock::now();
     if (interval.count() > 0) {
       std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(updateThreadMutex_);
-      updateThreadCondVar_.wait_for(lock, interval);
+      updateThreadCondVar_.wait_for(
+          lock, interval, [this] { return stopFlag_.load(); });
     }
     if (stopFlag_) {
       break;
